    "body": "pulse task #2903 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:b9df416120763dca0a58f310eb55ced9 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2903: Sampler MVP: play MIDI and Arrange/Console clips through the sample\n\nOperation: b9df416120763dca0a58f310eb55ced9\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nTarget: loaded Sampler makes correct audio from MIDI keyboard and both Arrange and Console clips. Acceptance: note pitch/velocity/tuning, gate/release and natural/loop lifetime obey supported laws; Stop, seek, clip retrigger, device/sample replacement and stale backend ACK do not leave stuck voices or install the wrong source. Preserve monitor/export behavior and actual callback ownership/allocation bounds. Demonstrate audible/rendered PCM through all three real entry paths plus focused Stop/seek/replacement tests; a standalone kernel or source-admission pass is insufficient.\n\nOwner: existing Native backend/producer and Local input/clip consumers, merger integration. Functional dependency is successful real sample load/admission. Keyboard/clip dispatch code and deterministic fixtures can proceed before final admission completes. Clear with actual composed backend publication and PCM tests, not a current-model label.\n\nSplit from overall acceptance #2789/canonical PR395, Playable Sampler MVP goal5. Preserve all existing implementation/history there. New intake linkage is a tracking shell only until a deliberate focused source handoff; do not copy existing edits into a competing branch or start another implementation. Record actual source/PR395 evidence and coordinate existing writer. This ticket is not complete merely because it was split or has a draft PR.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
